// expect-error: NITPICK-TAINT-001
// expect-error-at: 40:54
// expect-error: NITPICK-TAINT-001
// expect-error-at: 41:38
// expect-error: NITPICK-TAINT-001
// expect-error-at: 45:18
// expect-error: NITPICK-TAINT-001
// expect-error-at: 49:17
// expect-error: NITPICK-TAINT-001
// expect-error-at: 55:27
// expect-error: NITPICK-TAINT-001
// expect-error-at: 58:64
// expect-error: NITPICK-TAINT-001
// expect-error-at: 59:49
// A `.value` OR `.err` READ OFF A VALUE NO BINDING HOLDS IS UNCHECKED (DEF-406, landing 175).
//
// `check_value_read`/`check_err_read` refuse a read whose `Result` is a field or
// parameter path (F-4) and license one on a bare local by its `is_error` test; a base
// that is NEITHER -- a call's result, a `move(...)`, a ternary's value -- fell out of
// both branches and was READ WITHOUT A CHECK: `mkerr().value` read a NULL plain
// pointer (MachineFault, a backstop only) or a fabricated 0, `mkok().err` a silent
// zero (173 == 174, exit 50 on every cell). The comment above the rule called binding
// "the idiom", but an idiom is enforced only if the other spelling is refused. Now
// it is: bind the value to a local first and test `is_error` on THAT (D-007). The
// legal shapes are in `tests/backend/programs/result_temporary_ok.npk`.
//
// ONE MORE FACE, found by the review of this landing (F5): a base reached through the
// pointer level the TYPER peels -- a pointer binding's automatic dereference (`p.value`
// is `(<-p).value` with the `<-` left off, D-006; exit 50 on 174 and on the first
// build) -- is the same read under an identifier's spelling, and refuses with the same
// message. (The review's F6, `o?.value` through an `Optional`, is closed one stage
// earlier: a `Result`'s members are computed, and `?.` reaches a struct's stored field
// only -- `NITPICK-TYPE-102`, DEF-408, `tests/types/rejection/safe_nav_derived.npk`.)
mod:result_temporary_read;
error:E5;
func:mkok = int64() { pass 7i64; };
func:mkerr = int64() { fail E5; };

// A call's result (t2).
func:call_value = int64() never fails { pass (mkerr().value); };
func:call_err = int32() { fail mkok().err; };
// A `move(...)` (t1).
func:move_value = int64() never fails {
    Result<int64>:r = mkerr();
    pass (move(r).value);
};
func:move_err = int32() {
    Result<int64>:r = mkok();
    fail move(r).err;
};
// A ternary's value (t3).
func:ternary_value = int64(bool:c) never fails {
    Result<int64>:a = mkerr();
    Result<int64>:b = mkerr();
    pass ((is (c) : a : b).value);
};
// A pointer binding's AUTOMATIC dereference (F5): `.` peels one pointer level (D-006).
func:ptr_value = int64(Result<int64>->:p) never fails { pass (p.value); };
func:ptr_err = int32(Result<int64>->:p) { fail p.err; };
